<title>ARGENTINA: Argentina postpones hydroelectric dam sale.</title>
<headline>Argentina postpones hydroelectric dam sale.</headline>
<dateline>BUENOS AIRES 1996-11-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The privatization of Argentina's Pichi Picun Leufu hydroelectric dam has been postponed one month until December 9, the Energy Secretariat said Monday.</p>
<p>The Secretariat gave no reasons for the postponement of the sale of the 261 MW dam in Neuquen province.</p>
<p>Companies which have bought the tender specifications include Argentine firms  Hidroelectrica El Chocon, CAPEX, and Perez Companc, as well as Entergy, and AES from the United States. U.S. firm Duke Power Co also bought the specifications as part of a consortium.</p>
<p>-- Jason Webb, Buenos Aires Newsroom +541 318-0655</p>
